    "narrative": "The Austin Waves face a condensed schedule today, leaving the lineup reliant on a handful of core pieces to bridge the gap while stars like **Kyle Tucker**, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, and **Gunnar Henderson** are off. **Sam Antonacci** leads the daily efficiency ratings at 54.47, benefiting significantly from his leadoff spot against Blubaugh. While Blubaugh presents a middle-of-the-road matchup, **Sam Antonacci**\u2019s ability to maximize plate appearances remains the primary driver of his value. **Jackson Merrill** follows closely at 52.97; despite a negative platoon split against the southpaw Matthew Boyd, his consistent high-contact profile keeps his floor stable, even if his speed-based utility is muted by Boyd\u2019s high efficiency at holding runners.\n\n**Miguel Vargas** rounds out the top trio with a 50.15 score, buoyed by his presence in the heart of the order. He provides a steady, if unspectacular, baseline, though his upside is somewhat tempered by a slight park penalty. Meanwhile, **Drake Baldwin** (48.14) and **Heliot Ramos** (47.81) represent marginal plays. **Drake Baldwin** is navigating a tougher matchup against Luzardo, and while his leadoff status provides a nice +10% boost to his projection, the SP skill of his opponent necessitates caution. **Heliot Ramos** remains in the UTIL slot; despite the platoon disadvantage against Tolle, his Park Factor adjustment of +4% keeps him just ahead of our remaining bench depth.\n\nThe most difficult decision today involved the rotation of our middle-tier depth players, as we aim to preserve our remaining game caps for the final push. **Andy Pages** and **Jordan Westburg** were the strongest candidates left on the bench; however, they ultimately yielded to the higher projected volume afforded to **Sam Antonacci** and **Drake Baldwin** at the top of the lineup. With **Luis Robert Jr.** remaining on the IL and no high-upside speed threats among the remaining reserves like **Nasim Nunez** or **Jacob Wilson**, we are playing for stability rather than aggression. Keep a close eye on the weather and late-inning lineup substitutions, as any shift in the batting order for **Drake Baldwin** could further depress his efficiency score against a pitcher of Luzardo\u2019s caliber.",
